1. Core — MIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything in this repository is MIT-licensed (see `LICENSE`) **except** the
seLe4n-integration components listed in section 2. The MIT core comprises:

  * crates/topo-core, topo-abi, topo-backend-posix, topo-arch, topo-stats,
    topo-control, topo-test-support
  * tools/size-class-gen, tools/trace-replay
  * xtask, tests (the test crate's own sources)
  * lean/TopoMalloc/** except the SeLe4n bridge (section 2)
  * include/** and all generated artifacts

The default, distributable TopoMalloc artifact (`libtopomalloc`, the POSIX
backend) is built **without** any GPL component and is therefore MIT-licensed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. seLe4n integration — GPL-3.0-or-later
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The seLe4n-integration components are licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (see
`sele4n/LICENSE` and `vendor/sele4n/LICENSE`), because they link or model the
GPLv3 seLe4n microkernel ABI (`hatter6822/seLe4n`, pinned per decision D8). They
are:

  * crates/topo-backend-sele4n  — Sele4nSim and (from M1) the Sele4nBackingProvider
  * lean/TopoMalloc/SeLe4n/**   — the Lean bridge model
  * sele4n/**                   — the resource-server component and adapters
  * vendor/sele4n/**            — the VENDORED, pinned seLe4n Rust ABI crates
                                  (`sele4n-types`, `sele4n-abi`, `sele4n-sys`),
                                  upstream GPL-3.0-or-later, copyright their
                                  authors; see `vendor/sele4n/LICENSE` (the full
                                  GPLv3 text) and `vendor/sele4n/PINNED_SHA`. They
                                  are an unmodified mirror produced by
                                  `scripts/vendor_sele4n.sh`, linked only by
                                  `topo-backend-sele4n --features real-abi`.

Building TopoMalloc with the `sele4n-sim` Cargo feature (e.g.
`libtopomalloc-sele4n`), or `topo-backend-sele4n` with `--features real-abi`
(which links the vendored ABI above), links these GPL components; the resulting
combined binary is therefore GPL-3.0-or-later. The MIT crates' own source files
are unchanged and remain MIT; only the combined work is GPL. The default,
distributable artifact enables neither feature and links no GPL code.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. SPDX policy (W0-12)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every source file carries an `SPDX-License-Identifier` header:

  * `MIT`                — core files
  * `GPL-3.0-or-later`   — the section-2 seLe4n-integration files

CI enforces this (`cargo xtask lint`). When adding a file under
`crates/topo-backend-sele4n`, `lean/TopoMalloc/SeLe4n`, or `sele4n/`, use the
`GPL-3.0-or-later` identifier; everywhere else use `MIT`.

Vendored upstream code under `vendor/` is **exempt** from this per-file policy
(the `xtask` SPDX gate skips `vendor/`): it carries its own upstream
`SPDX-License-Identifier` headers and a complete license text
(`vendor/sele4n/LICENSE`), and its provenance is pinned in
`vendor/sele4n/PINNED_SHA`. We do not re-license or re-header third-party code.

